## Project Structure

[Describe the architecture. If using Clean Architecture, dependencies always point inward:
`presentation → application → domain`, `infrastructure → application → domain`.]

```
src/
├── domain/              # Zero external dependencies
│   ├── entities/        # Aggregate roots and child entities
│   ├── value-objects/   # Immutable, validated value types
│   ├── events/          # Domain events (past tense, immutable)
│   ├── services/        # Stateless domain logic spanning aggregates
│   └── repositories/    # Repository interfaces (ports) — NO implementations
│
├── application/         # Depends on domain only
│   ├── use-cases/       # One class per use case
│   ├── ports/           # Input/output port interfaces
│   └── dtos/            # Data transfer objects
│
├── infrastructure/      # Depends on application and domain
│   ├── repositories/    # Repository implementations (adapters)
│   ├── persistence/     # Migrations, schema, seed data
│   └── external/        # Third-party adapters
│
└── presentation/        # Depends on application only
    └── http/            # Controllers, routes, request/response mapping

test/
├── unit/                # Pure unit tests — domain (no mocks) + application (mock ports)
├── integration/         # Real datastore via containers
└── e2e/                 # End-to-end against the full stack
```

See `.claude/planning/architecture/layer-map.md` for the dependency matrix and port/adapter registry.

## API Contract Workflow

[PROJECT_NAME] follows a **contract-first** workflow so frontend and backend ship in parallel.
The schemas in [CONTRACT_PACKAGE] are the single source of truth for every endpoint — they drive
backend validation, frontend types, the OpenAPI document, mock data, and contract tests.

**Rule of thumb**: an endpoint exists when its contract merges, not when its handler ships.

| Step | Output | Who |
|---|---|---|
| 1. Contract PR | schemas + OpenAPI metadata + mocks + registry entry | whoever picks up the feature |
| 2. FE branch (parallel) | screen built against the mock + generated types | FE |
| 3. BE branch (parallel) | handler + use case; response parsed against the schema | BE |
| 4. Cutover | FE drops the mock handler; it stays as a test fixture | FE |

**See also**: [`.claude/rules/api-contracts.md`](./.claude/rules/api-contracts.md), and the ADR
that records this decision for your project.

